.pf/artifacts/core-a01-a11-20260911\prepare_remaining.py:13:    ('a08-jsonrpc', ['tools/pf_runtime/mcp_server.py', 'tools/smoke_mcp_jsonrpc_validation.py'], '''Fix A08 in native stdio MCP. Current respond/main accepts jsonrpc 1.0 and coerces list params/arguments to {} and responds to notifications. Validate JSON-RPC 2.0 envelope, method/id types (bool is not numeric ID), params and tools/call arguments using existing advertised tool schema constraints before dispatch. Preserve missing optional args/defaults and valid clients. Errors: parse -32700; invalid envelope -32600; invalid params/schema -32602; unknown method -32601. Valid notifications never emit responses including tools/call errors, but valid mutating notifications retain the chosen spec-compliant dispatch behavior. Distinguish id absent from explicit null. Use local JSONRPC/MCP docs or existing tests, no new third-party dependency. Regression sends real newline-framed requests to source native stdio MCP with disposable workplace, tests malformed JSON recovery, wrong protocol/method/id, params and arguments arrays/scalars, required/type/unknown arguments, valid initialize/list/tool call, notification silence using subsequent sentinel response. A fake runtime can supplement dispatch count but is not sole protocol proof. Do not change business/session logic.''')
.pf/artifacts/core-a01-a11-20260911\a08-jsonrpc-brief.md:5:Fix A08 in native stdio MCP. Current respond/main accepts jsonrpc 1.0 and coerces list params/arguments to {} and responds to notifications. Validate JSON-RPC 2.0 envelope, method/id types (bool is not numeric ID), params and tools/call arguments using existing advertised tool schema constraints before dispatch. Preserve missing optional args/defaults and valid clients. Errors: parse -32700; invalid envelope -32600; invalid params/schema -32602; unknown method -32601. Valid notifications never emit responses including tools/call errors, but valid mutating notifications retain the chosen spec-compliant dispatch behavior. Distinguish id absent from explicit null. Use local JSONRPC/MCP docs or existing tests, no new third-party dependency. Regression sends real newline-framed requests to source native stdio MCP with disposable workplace, tests malformed JSON recovery, wrong protocol/method/id, params and arguments arrays/scalars, required/type/unknown arguments, valid initialize/list/tool call, notification silence using subsequent sentinel response. A fake runtime can supplement dispatch count but is not sole protocol proof. Do not change business/session logic.
